      "label": "Right eye examination: best spectacle-corrected visual acuity 20/20, normal conjunctiva and adnexa, cornea with normal luster and even surface, no distinct arcus senilis, normal anterior stroma; 4 symmetric complete concentric ring-shaped opacities in posterior corneal stroma, outermost ring ~4mm from limbus, vertical diameters 6.0mm, 4.8mm, 4.5mm, 3.6mm; ring surfaces smooth without deposits, pigmentation, or serrations; peripheral cornea with posterior crocodile shagreen; corneal sensations normal.",
      "task_id": "case-92",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-20T05:55:21.701+00:00",
